{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And when it rested.</b> Like ונוח הארון, written with heh like the heh of אהלה, for the letters אהו״י interchange." "<b>Return, YHWH.</b> Rabbi Judah the first grammarian said: every שב whose root is from the derivation of תשובה is an intransitive verb and does not occur in the binyan qal unless its accent is in rest and quietness, like בשובה ונחת תושעון; so too שובה ה׳ רבבות אלפי ישראל — that He may give rest, and they not be troubled by an enemy. And know that רבבה is from the root רב, and the meaning is like רבבה כצמח השדה נתתיך. And it is possible that ten thousand is so called because it is a large number; therefore the word רבבות is in construct with אלפי. And Moses prayed that HaShem give rest and quiet to all Israel, and if they are many [all the more]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "The final phrase 'ואם הם רבים' is rendered hyper-literally; the logical connection to the preceding prayer is left as Ibn Ezra's terse concluding gesture."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:09.089129556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}